  "title": "Nebra Sky Disc",
  "summary": "The Nebra Sky Disc is a bronze disc 32 centimetres across, about 3,600 years old, showing the sun or full moon, a crescent moon and 32 golden stars. Detectorists illegally dug it up on the Mittelberg hill near Nebra in 1999; police recovered it in Basel in 2002. It was added to UNESCO’s Memory of the World register in June 2013.",
